ronavirus  that also doesn't go down well at the  moment with the british public as well  may i say  so is this likely to have any  consequences for mr johnson  well it doesn't look good because at the  next and next and the next week we are  having  our local elections scottish elections  for the scottish parliament  so it does uh give the conservative  party quite  a lot of headache at the moment and they  will see if if their poles are dropping  as a result of this  i think it's the sort of drip drip of  allegations of of  sleaze because the refurbishment issue  of the flat is not the only  um point that came up there were other  allegations that business people like  for example uh sir james dyson the  businessman had  access to uh boris johnson and private  messages and that boris johnson  promised to fix a tax issue that the  businessmen were facing  also lobbying by david cameron the  former prime minister on behalf of a  financial  company lobbying with the government and  so there are quite a few allegations  that are beginning  to the the people are beginning to  notice it  uh but i think the the most worrying one  for the brit you know in the eyes of the  british public i would think  is there are the remarks the alleged  remarks of boris johnson when it comes  to the victims of the coronavirus crisis  um allegedly a very flippant remark that  he would rather see more bodies pile up  than go into another lockdown  i think this remark is being seen by by  people  definitely as very inappropriate if it  was true  bernie madison london thank you
 

